function addContent(content) {
    var existingContent = document.getElementById('content').innerHTML;
    document.getElementById('content').innerHTML = existingContent + content;
}

// Example usage
addContent("<p>This is some new content.</p>");
```

In this code, the `addContent` function takes a `content` parameter, which is the HTML content you want to add to the existing content. It retrieves the current innerHTML of an element with the ID 'content', concatenates the new content with the existing content, and then sets the innerHTML of the element back to the updated value.

To use this function, simply call it with the desired content as an argument, like in the example where `<p>This is some new content.</p>` is added.

